<title>JAPAN: Green Cross up on HIV gene therapy approval.</title>
<headline>Green Cross up on HIV gene therapy approval.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-03-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Green Cross Corp shares rose on Friday after a government advisory panel approved the use of an anti-HIV gene therapy product, HIV-IT(V), brokers said.</p>
<p>As of 0448 GMT, the shares were up 30 yen at 500, the 10th largest percentage gainer on the first section of the Tokyo bourse.  </p>
<p>HIV-IT(V) is now under development by a division of U.S.-based Chiron Corp, a Green Cross spokesman said.</p>
<p>The company is now waiting for the Ministry of Health and Welfare's formal approval, he said. The new treatment was jointly developed with Kumamoto University in Japan.</p>
